{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_012QqwKqZUThAeecc5D8XrYc","type":"tool_result","content":"/private/var/folders/6v/yk9bzvrn5zx0kxll7d4szzb80000gn/T/brace-challenger-5el392u9\ntotal 24\ndrwx------@     4 brenn  staff     128 Oct  2 17:49 .\ndrwx------@ 13620 brenn  staff  435840 Oct  2 17:49 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x@    14 brenn  staff     448 Oct  2 12:21 agent\n-rw-r--r--@     1 brenn  staff    9879 Oct  2 17:49 sheet.md\n# Gap hunt: B03 — Credential lifetime and handling\n\nA reviewer couldn't decide whether this item is met. **Your job is to find out whether any\ncheck below is false in this codebase.** The reviewer's partial answers and the code they\nlooked at are shown. Read the code, and open the repo files the checks point to.\n\nFor each check, decide:\n- **fails**: you found the line that makes it false (a missing control, a bypass, a\n  value never used, an exception that continues, a filter that lets something through).\n  Quote that line;\n- **holds**: you found the code that makes it true in every case;\n- **unclear**: you can't tell from this repo.\n\n**The requirement for B03:** Issue short-lived credentials from a managed identity or secrets service. Keep long-lived secrets out of prompts, images, and checked-in config. Where the service supports it, bind tokens to their holder (mTLS, DPoP, or workload proof tokens). Then a copied token won't work from another machine. Don't use fixed API keys when short-lived or federated credentials are available. Show that credentials expire and rotate, and explain why you chose their lifetime.\n\nIf a check fails, also copy the words from this requirement that the code breaks into\n`violates`. Then write your answer (format at the end).\n\n\n## B03.1\n\n**Check:** Credentials are fetched at run time from a managed identity or secrets service, not fixed API keys, where short-lived or federated credentials are available.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find credential setup (`AssumeRole`, IRSA, Workload Identity, Managed Identity, Vault, `os.environ`, `process.env`). 2) Check each credential is fetched at run time. 3) Answer no if a fixed key (`AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID`, `API_KEY` in a Secret or env) is used for a service that offers federated or short-lived credentials, or code falls back to a static key when the managed source fails.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:36 — \"new GetSecretValueCommand({ SecretId:\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Per-clinic client secrets are fetched at run time from Secrets Manager; pods use IRSA and a projected token.\n\n`src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` lines 24–48 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n  24      },\n  25    });\n  26  }\n  27  \n  28  type Token = { value: string; exp: number };\n  29  const tokens = new Map<string, Token>();\n  30  \n  31  async function ehrToken(clinicId: string, scope: string): Promise<string> {\n  32    const cacheKey = `${clinicId}|${scope}`;\n  33    const hit = tokens.get(cacheKey);\n  34    if (hit && hit.exp - 30_000 > Date.now()) return hit.value;\n  35  \n  36>   const sec = await sm.send(new GetSecretValueCommand({ SecretId: `clinic-agent/ehr/${clinicId}` }));\n  37    const { client_id, client_secret, token_url } = JSON.parse(sec.SecretString ?? \"{}\");\n  38    const res = await fetch(token_url, {\n  39      method: \"POST\",\n  40      headers: { \"content-type\": \"application/x-www-form-urlencoded\" },\n  41      body: new URLSearchParams({ grant_type: \"client_credentials\", client_id, client_secret, scope }),\n  42    });\n  43    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`EHR token request failed: ${res.status}`);\n  44    const body = (await res.json()) as { access_token: string; expires_in: number };\n  45    tokens.set(cacheKey, { value: body.access_token, exp: Date.now() + body.expires_in * 1000 });\n  46    return body.access_token;\n  47  }\n  48  \n```\n\n## B03.2\n\n**Check:** Credential lifetime and rotation are set in config to bounded values.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Search for lifetime and rotation settings (`DurationSeconds`, `ttl`, `expires_in`, `max_ttl`, rotation job or policy). 2) Check each credential the agent uses has a bounded value. 3) Answer no if any credential has no expiry, no rotation, or an unbounded or very long value. Answer unknown if lifetimes are set in an identity provider outside this repo.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** infra/terraform/main.tf:166 — \"resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** Token lifetimes are bounded in the repo (workload token 900 s at deployment.yaml:111, EHR access tokens 5 min, IRSA sessions 3600 s at iam.tf:5). The static vendor secrets (EHR client secret, payments key, SMS token, SMS signing secret) are created in main.tf:161-178 with no rotation resource anywhere in the repo. Rotation may be set outside Terraform.\n\n`infra/terraform/main.tf` lines 154–178 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n 154      bucket_arn          = aws_s3_bucket.audit.arn\n 155      prefix              = \"audit/dt=!{timestamp:yyyy-MM-dd}/\"\n 156      error_output_prefix = \"audit-errors/!{firehose:error-output-type}/\"\n 157      buffering_interval  = 60\n 158    }\n 159  }\n 160  \n 161  resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"ehr\" {\n 162    for_each = toset(concat(var.clinic_ids, [\"_catalog\"]))\n 163    name     = \"clinic-agent/ehr/${each.key}\"\n 164  }\n 165  \n 166> resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"payments\" {\n 167    for_each = toset(var.clinic_ids)\n 168    name     = \"clinic-agent/payments/${each.key}\"\n 169  }\n 170  \n 171  resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"sms\" {\n 172    for_each = toset(var.clinic_ids)\n 173    name     = \"clinic-agent/sms/${each.key}\"\n 174  }\n 175  \n 176  resource \"aws_secretsmanager_secret\" \"sms_signing\" {\n 177    name = \"clinic-agent/sms-signing\"\n 178  }\n```\n\n## B03.3\n\n**Check:** No long-lived secrets appear in prompts, Dockerfiles or image layers, or checked-in config.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Search prompt templates, Dockerfiles (`ENV`, `ARG`, `COPY .env`), `.env*`, `*.yaml`, `*.tfvars`, `.mcp.json` `env` blocks for key-like literals (`sk-`, `AKIA`, `token:`, `password:`). 2) Check prompt-building code for env values inserted into messages. 3) Answer no if any real secret is checked in, baked into an image, or placed in a prompt; `.gitignore` listing a file does not count if it is committed.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** Dockerfile:12 — \"ENV NODE_ENV=production\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** No long-lived secret literal in prompts, Dockerfile, k8s or config.\n\n`Dockerfile` lines 1–22 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n   1  # syntax=docker/dockerfile:1.7\n   2  FROM node:22.11-bookworm-slim@sha256:3f1a8d2c9b7e4f6a5d0c8b1e2f3a4b5c6d7e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a AS build\n   3  WORKDIR /app\n   4  COPY package.json package-lock.json ./\n   5  RUN npm ci --ignore-scripts\n   6  COPY tsconfig.json ./\n   7  COPY src ./src\n   8  RUN npm run build && npm prune --omit=dev\n   9  \n  10  FROM gcr.io/distroless/nodejs22-debian12:nonroot@sha256:9b2e4c6a8d0f1e3c5a7b9d1f3e5c7a9b1d3f5e7c9a1b3d5f7e9c1a3b5d7f9e1c\n  11  WORKDIR /app\n  12> ENV NODE_ENV=production \\\n  13      CLINIC_AGENT_ROOT=/app\n  14  COPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/node_modules ./node_modules\n  15  COPY --from=build --chown=65532:65532 /app/dist ./dist\n  16  COPY --chown=65532:65532 package.json ./\n  17  COPY --chown=65532:65532 prompts ./prompts\n  18  COPY --chown=65532:65532 config ./config\n  19  COPY --chown=65532:65532 release ./release\n  20  USER 65532:65532\n  21  EXPOSE 8080\n  22  CMD [\"dist/server.js\"]\n```\n\n## B03.4\n\n**Check:** Where the service supports it, tokens are bound to their holder with mTLS, DPoP, or workload proof tokens.\n\n**How to verify:** 1) Find token and client setup for each service (`mTLS`, `client_cert`, `DPoP`, `cert-bound`, SPIFFE). 2) Check whether the service supports holder binding. 3) Answer no if a supporting service uses plain bearer tokens. Answer unknown if support depends on a provider outside this repo and nothing states it.\n\n**Reviewer's evidence:** src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts:18 — \"checkServerIdentity: (_host: string, cert: PeerCertificate) => {\"\n\n**Reviewer's note:** README says mTLS, but the code only pins the server certificate (ehr-mcp.ts:16-25) and sends bearer tokens. No client certificate, DPoP or cert-bound token is configured. Whether the EHR, payments and SMS providers support holder binding is not stated here.\n\n`src/integrations/ehr-mcp.ts` lines 6–30 (cited lines marked >):\n```\n   6  import { env } from \"../config.js\";\n   7  import type { ConfiguredServer } from \"../tools/registry.js\";\n   8  import type { ServerMeta } from \"../tools/metadata-scan.js\";\n   9  \n  10  // EHR access goes through the EHR vendor's MCP server. Each clinic has its own OAuth client in the\n  11  // EHR, so tokens are clinic-scoped on the EHR side. Client secrets live in Secrets Manager under\n  12  // clinic-agent/ehr/<clinicId>; access tokens last 5 minutes and are cached until 30 s before expiry.\n  13  \n  14  const sm = new SecretsManagerClient({ region: env.region });\n  15  \n  16  function pinnedDispatcher(server: ConfiguredServer): Agent {\n  17    const expected = server.tlsCertSha256.toLowerCase();\n  18>   return new Agent({\n  19      connect: {\n  20        checkServerIdentity: (_host: string, cert: PeerCertificate) => {\n  21          const got = cert.fingerprint256.replace(/:/g, \"\").toLowerCase();\n  22          return got === expected ? undefined : new Error(`EHR MCP certificate mismatch: ${got}`);\n  23        },\n  24      },\n  25    });\n  26  }\n  27  \n  28  type Token = { value: string; exp: number };\n  29  const tokens = new Map<string, Token>();\n  30  \n```\n\n## Your answer\n\nWrite this JSON to B03.verdict.json in this folder (or put it in verdicts.json under \"B03\"):\n```json\n{\"verdict\": \"upheld | failed | unclear\",\n \"checks\": [{\"id\": \"B03.1\", \"result